<p>You can change the one click preset display order, delete a one click 
 preset, and change its name and comment.</p>
<p>You can also load a printing preferences settings file as a one click 
 preset and save a registered one click preset as a file.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>You cannot change the names and comments of the system-provided one click presets.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="list" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">One Click Preset List:</span></p>
<p>Displays the registered one click preset names, comments, and status 
 in the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="up" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Up</span></p>
<p>Moves the one click preset display order up.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="down" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Down</span></p>
<p>Moves the one click preset display order down.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="delete" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span></p>
<p>Deletes the selected one click preset.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="import" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Import...</span></p>
<p>You can load a printing preferences settings file provided by an administrator 
 as a one click preset.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="export" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Export...</span></p>
<p>You can save a registered one click preset as a file.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="name" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">One Click Preset Name:</span></p>
<p>You can change the name of the one click preset selected in the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="comment" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Comment:</span></p>
<p>You can change the comment of the one click preset selected in the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
